    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08956v1</id>
    <title>Discovery Opportunities with Gravitational Waves -- TASI 2024 Lecture Notes</title>
    <updated>2024-09-13T16:20:42Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08956v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2409.08956v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Recent advancements in gravitational wave astronomy hold the promise of a completely new way to explore our Universe. These lecture notes aim to provide a concise but self-contained introduction to key concepts of gravitational wave physics, with a focus on the opportunities to explore fundamental physics in transient gravitational wave signals and stochastic gravitational wave background searches.CERN-TH-2024-152</summary>
